WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Just in time for #@$%virus comes, the perfect film showing the importance of social distancing

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:14.129
Yes, Netflix's The Platform -- or, as I like to call it, The Vertical Snowpiercer -- is a uniquely wild horror film that makes me thankful

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.130
I'm not fighting over toilet paper

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.320
In this video,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:25.859
we'll be taking a deep dive into the film's cryptic ending, and what exactly it was trying to say about our society

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:30.239
Hint: it's not good. So grab something to eat because here we go

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.689
Welcome to floor zero, the top floor of an over 300 plus levels structure known affectionately as the "hole"

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.219
It's here that a selection of meticulously prepared meals are cooked for the exactly

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:48.479
666 guests. Yes, 666. If that is an assign the hole isn't the friendliest of places

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.500
We know this is the number since at the end of the film we see the final floor is

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.579
333 and there are two people per floor. Meet Goreng,

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:03.718
our film's protagonist, who wakes up on level 48. But notice before he wakes he hears his cellmate say the following over darkness

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:19.209
This is actually the first line in the entire film and it's arguably the most important. There are those at the top, who are

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:25.990
content with the way things are; those at the bottom, who want change but lack the means to do so; and those who fall.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.619
This last line -- that those who fall -- actually has two meanings:

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:37.359
first, the actual people who fall over the legend and die and, secondly, people like Goreng and his future cellmate, Baharat, who willingly

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.560
descend in order to create change

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.080
So what this quote really means is that these three types of people are those who don't want to change,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.469
those who want to but can't do it, and those who risk everything,

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.020
even death, to change it. Goreng spends much of the first-act figuring out how this place operates --

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:59.379
just like we, the viewer, do -- and in so doing we create a subconscious bond with him even asking ourselves:

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.170
what would we do if we were in that situation?

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:09.220
To make matters worse, Goreng's platform-mate is a greedy old man by the name of Trimagasi, a man who unlike Goreng. Is a

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.219
prisoner for having thrown his TV out the window and

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:19.390
accidentally murdering someone. They gave him the option of either spending his time at the psych-hospital or spending a year in the hole

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.969
Goreng, on the other hand, is here voluntarily

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:28.899
He tells Trimagasi that he's here for six months in exchange for a college diploma and thought this would be a good way to

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.540
quit smoking

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.089
It's important to note here that those on the outside don't really know what goes on in the hole

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.869
Even the character Imoguiri, who interviewed candidates for the hole, didn't exactly know what went on there. What's important here?

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.580
Is that the hole promises a prize for those who endure it. For Imoguiri,

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.029
it's the cure for her cancer; Trimagasi, his freedom; and

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:55.059
Goring, his diploma. These, for the most part, are empty promises since most died before they're done their time,

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.810
but it's the analogy to

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:02.980
capitalism and its promise that, if you work hard, you can get what you dream of, that also falls flat. Many believe in capitalism,

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.889
But are held back by a system which is cruel and unjust --

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:11.259
just like the "hole" --, but they cling to the hope that things will get better. As the Imoguiri says later,

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.660
things won't change unless there is a spontaneous

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.799
solidarity, but we'll get to what that means in a bit. Every day a

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:24.599
platform descends containing a myriad of food and depending which level you're on the amount. The food is also dictated by the

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:31.859
preferences of those in the hole. For example, one of the interview questions, Goreng is asked is what his favorite food is. Later on,

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.769
We'll see escargot is on the platform, which is what he chose

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:41.699
As the platform descends deeper and deeper, less food is available for those at the bottom. Until around level a hundred,

00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:47.009
where there's almost no food at all. Leaving over 400 people to starve, who have to make drastic

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:50.759
decisions, such as eating their partners. While the platform is there,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:50.939
however,

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:58.319
the prisoners are given one minute to stuff themselves, as much as possible, before it descends to the next level. If anyone hoards food,

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.980
extreme heat or cold

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.989
fills the level killing inhabitants until the food is put back. Trimagasi tells Goreng that, because they're on level 47,

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.239
94 people have eaten before them. He's almost done his time and notes that, every month,

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:19.379
the prisoners are randomly placed on a new level. Trimagasi has been as high as level 8 and as low as a hundred and

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.979
thirty-two. Each prisoner is also allowed one item on their journey

00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:27.689
Goreng is laughed at since he brings a copy of Don Quixote, instead of something practical,

00:04:27.789 --> 00:04:29.400
likeTrimagasi's knife

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:36.510
Not only does Goreng resemble Don Quixote, but his journey within the platform mimics the thematic journey of Quixote as well

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.179
The book was revolutionary for its time in the way

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.659
it emphasized the disparities between class and worth. The

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.919
aristocrats were seen as thoughtless,

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:52.109
unkind and frivolous; while the peasant Sancho, wise and thoughtful. We see this system play out in the film through the greed of those at

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:57.599
the top contrasted with characters like Goreng whose thoughtfulness forces him to act for the good of the hole

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:03.150
Having Goreng paired with Trimagasi shows how individual greed reinforces a corrupt system

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:10.349
The first thing Goreng mentions is that they should ration the food so that those below can have enough. Trimagasi, being the complete foil

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:15.149
to Goreng, responds by pissing on the people below him. Instead of helping those at the bottom,

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:22.139
people in this movie get literally pissed and shit on -- I can't show that clip --, much like how many billionaires and corporations

00:05:22.419 --> 00:05:24.280
exploit, piss and shit --

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:30.929
metaphorically, of course -- on the poor. Things begin to change with the introduction of Miharu, a woman who descends on the platform in her search

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.860
for her child

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:39.360
The Japanese translation of Miharu is to "open one's eyes wide" and it's through her struggle that Goreng opens his eyes to the injustice

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:40.979
perpetrated by this system

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:47.218
In fact, to accentuate this point, Miharu doesn't even speak. The end of act one puts Goreng in a tough situation

00:05:47.409 --> 00:05:51.989
A full month has passed and he awakens tied up on a new floor, level

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:55.408
171. This means almost certain death for the two men

00:05:55.409 --> 00:06:00.149
So Trimagasi, being a veteran, has tied Goreng and will feast on him slowly and

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:04.379
even feed Goering his own flesh in order to survive. For Trimagasi,

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:08.218
this is a perfectly normal and rational thing to do given the situation

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:12.299
He justifies it by saying it's not him who's doing these crimes,

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:18.060
but the people above him. The system has forced him to do something drastic in order to survive, much

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.289
like how many people in the real world do illegal things in order to survive as well

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:25.770
And as Trimagasi cuts into his first piece of Goreng's flesh,

00:06:25.779 --> 00:06:32.159
he's saved by Miharu only to wake up next month on level 33 with a new partner. This is Imoguiri

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.810
She's an idealist, like Goreng, but lacks the fire it takes to actually create change

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.509
She spends weeks yelling at the people below her, pleading with them to ration. So there will be food left for those below

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:42.990
These

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:48.870
please fall on deaf ears until goring threatens to shit on their food. Since Imoguiri used to work for the administration,

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:55.589
the company that runs the vertical self-management center -- a.k.a. The Hole --, she has some inside information

00:06:55.750 --> 00:07:00.929
No one under 16 is allowed there, and she believes she knows why the system is there to begin with

00:07:01.029 --> 00:07:03.838
It's a test to see what it takes to create a

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:11.609
revolution of change. A change that will be the result of what she calls quote a "spontaneous sense of solidarity". Of course, Goreng retorts:

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.919
Even going so far as to conjecture:

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:33.159
Imoguiri item, her pet Ramses II, is named after the greatest Egyptian pharaoh of the new kingdom. The dog's death, later in the film,

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.479
symbolic of the death of greatness, the death of the idea that we can unite

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:42.670
everyone under one strong banner. A month passes and Goreng awakens to find that

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:48.580
Imoguiri has killed herself after finding out they've been placed on level 202 -- basically a death sentence

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.720
No food makes it this far down

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.970
He has to eat pages of his book as well as her body in order to stay alive

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:59.079
Eventually making it to his final month with a new platform-mate named Baharat

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:04.720
Baharat is smart and brought a rope as his item, believing that, if he could just make it close to the top,

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.759
he could escape. But this plan implies that those at the top are willing to help and that is definitely

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:14.740
not the case, with the people above him literally shitting on him as he attempts to climb

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:20.199
Goreng and Baharat devise a plan to descend along with the platform and evenly distribute the food themselves

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:24.490
Even going so far as to withhold food from the people in the first 50 levels,

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:27.669
so that those at the bottom can have their fair share. They even

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.639
mercilessly beat those who try to take any food from them

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:36.460
It isn't until they descend and meet someone who is only known as the Wise Old Man that there told the only way they can

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:40.660
Make real lasting change is with a symbol -- in this case, a message

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.209
If a message can make it all the way to level zero,

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:49.690
maybe even those cooks up there will understand what is happening below. And what perfect message then panna cotta

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:50.650
Well,

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:57.429
it's not so much the panna cotta, but the defiant act of leaving a dish untouched. But, as will later find, there's an even better

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:03.339
message. As they descend to the final level, Goreng saves Miharu from an attacker, just like she saved him earlier

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:09.429
She doesn't make it, but he finds something more valuable: a small child, the thing Miharu was searching for all along

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:15.340
Imoguiri told us that Miharu never had a child and that people under 16 can't be put in a hole

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:20.739
So this means that: a) that child is simply a symbol for change; or b) is real and that the

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:24.190
administration is into some real effed up shit that will then cause

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:30.040
change. Baharat and Goreng give the child the panna cotta in what is a selfless act contradicting the greed

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:35.469
we've seen throughout the film. Baharat succumbs to his wounds, leaving Goreng to take the child to the final level

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:42.160
He's realized that the child is the message after all. He also quotes Don Quixote here to hammer home the notion

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.510
that wealth is not measured by what you own, but by how you spend it

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:59.889
The spending it well here is referring to spending it on others, sharing it if you will

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:02.169
He places the child on the platform and it

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:08.410
ascends to the top. A film that started at level zero ends at the bottom only to come full circle to the top. Now we

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:13.930
don't see what happens to Goreng, but we can assume, just like how Don Quixote dies at the end of the book, so too

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:18.699
does Goreng. Don Quixote's death signals the end of an arrow, the end of knights and

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.610
chivalry, and the Goreng's, the end of the corrupt and greedy

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:28.269
nature of the hole. The child is the spark, the message if you will that will change the system and call people to action

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:34.899
It will unify people to work together toward a common goal and break the complacency that prevents change

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.930
The platform isn't just a horror film with a unique premise

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:42.549
It's one that asks tough philosophical questions about how we function as a society

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:48.219
So I leave it up to you: if you were in the hole, what would you do? And more importantly, what would you order?

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.360
Thanks for watching, everyone

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.490
Please, make sure to give the video a like and subscribe with that fell on to get notified as soon as one of my videos

